# OxiBonsai CLI — copy to `.env` (auto-loaded from the current directory or any
# parent directory) to omit flags.
# Precedence: --flag  >  shell env  >  .env  >  built-in default.
#
# Every entry below is commented out: uncomment only what you set. A `.env`
# left behind in a parent directory of a checkout is loaded by every
# `oxibonsai` run beneath it and silently changes what those runs do, so
# delete it when you no longer want its values. The full list of variables
# (with defaults) is in docs/CLI.md, "Environment variables".

# ── models (`oxibonsai run` / `chat` / `serve` / `info` / `benchmark` / `eval`) ──
# GGUF model (omit --model when set). Works for every supported model,
# including the Bonsai 2 27B files (see docs/models.md).
#OXI_MODEL=/path/to/model.gguf
# Tokenizer json or dir (optional; omit --tokenizer when set)
#OXI_TOKENIZER=/path/to/tokenizer.json

# ── Bonsai 2 27B (`qwen35` hybrid) ──
# The vision projector has no environment fallback: pass `--mmproj <file>`
# (and `--image <file>` on run/chat) on the command line.
# The three remote-image variables below are read only by a command given
# `--mmproj`; a text-only run/chat/serve never consults them.
# Fallback for --allow-image-url-fetch (1/true/yes/on): fetch remote `http(s)`
# image references (run/chat --image, serve image_url) from public addresses
# only. Unset, they are refused with `image_url_fetch_disabled` and nothing is
# opened. Keep it off on a public server unless clients need it. The flag wins.
#OXI_ALLOW_IMAGE_URL_FETCH=1
# Fallback for --image-url-timeout-ms: the per-image fetch deadline in
# milliseconds (resolve, connect, TLS and the whole body; default 10000).
# Read only once remote fetching is opted in.
#OXI_IMAGE_URL_TIMEOUT_MS=10000
# Fallback for --image-url-allow-host (comma-separated host[:port] entries,
# added to the flag's): hosts exempt from the public-address rule, such as an
# intranet image store. Needs the opt-in above: with --mmproj, set without it
# is a start-up error.
#OXI_IMAGE_URL_ALLOW_HOSTS=images.intranet:8080
# Fallback for `serve --media-path`: the only directory `file://` image
# references may read from.
#OXI_MEDIA_PATH=/path/to/media
# Which of the three on-disk layouts that share ggml type id 42 to read
# (d-first | qs-first | g64). Leave unset: the loader decides from the file.
#OXI_FORCE_Q2_LAYOUT=d-first
# `oxibonsai pull`: alternative HuggingFace repositories for the Bonsai 2 files
# and a mirror base URL.
#OXI_BONSAI2_REPO=prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf
#OXI_BONSAI2_DEV_REPO=prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf-dev
#OXIBONSAI_HF_BASE_URL=https://huggingface.co
# Opt-in INT8 dot-product CPU tier (lossy; never selected by default):
# int8-scalar | neon-int8 | neon-dot | neon-i8mm | avx512-vnni
#OXIBONSAI_KERNEL_TIER=neon-dot

# ── imagen (`oxibonsai image`) ──
# DiT FLUX.2 Klein ternary GGUF
#OXI_DIT_GGUF=/path/to/flux2-klein-dit.gguf
# VAE decoder weights: the canonical FLUX.2 AutoencoderKLFlux2
# `vae/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors` file (loaded natively, no Python
# dump step — preferred) OR a directory of per-tensor f32 `.npy` files.
# Auto-detected: a `.safetensors` file uses the safetensors loader; a directory
# uses the `.npy` loader.
#OXI_VAE_WEIGHTS=/path/to/vae/diffusion_pytorch_model.safetensors
# Text encoder: native 2.1GB 4-bit MLX safetensors (preferred over the f32 npy dir)
#OXI_TE_4BIT=/path/to/text_encoder-mlx-4bit/model.safetensors
# Tokenizer dir (defaults to the TE safetensors' parent dir if unset)
#OXI_TE_TOKENIZER_DIR=/path/to/text_encoder-mlx-4bit

# ── GPU acceleration (imagen pipeline) ──
# DiT attention (flash-attention kernel) — ON by default on Apple Silicon / Metal.
# Set to 0 to force CPU fallback.
#OXI_DIT_ATTN_GPU=0
# VAE decoder convolutions — ON by default on Apple Silicon / Metal.
# Set to 0 to force CPU fallback.
#OXI_VAE_GPU=0
# Text-encoder (TE) GPU acceleration — OFF by default.
# On Apple Silicon the CPU SIMD path is faster; on Windows / NVIDIA CUDA this
# flag may give a significant speedup — try enabling it if TE feels slow.
#OXI_TE_GPU=1

# ── server concurrency ──
# Engine replicas (`oxibonsai serve` and `oxibonsai-serve`). Default:
# min(4, CPU cores) for a dense model on a CPU tier, and 1 on a Metal tier or
# for a Bonsai 2 `qwen35` model on any executor. An explicit value is honoured
# on the CPU and capped at OXIBONSAI_METAL_MAX_SESSIONS on Metal; a CUDA-only
# build clamps to 1 (see the pool-size table in docs/CLI.md). Replicas share
# one token-embedding table, so each extra replica only adds a KV cache.
#OXIBONSAI_ENGINE_POOL_SIZE=4
# Metal session ceiling the pool is sized against (default 4; a memory bound).
#OXIBONSAI_METAL_MAX_SESSIONS=4
